  "question": {
    "text": "In Bohr series of lines of hydrogen spectrum, the third line from the red end corresponds to which one of the following inter-orbit jumps of the electron for Bohr orbits in an atom of hydrogen",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cIKGH",
      "text": "\n$5 \\rightarrow 2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HPwnj",
      "text": "\n$4 \\rightarrow 1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wMTFK",
      "text": "\n$2 \\rightarrow 5$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "O9JnA",
      "text": "\n$3 \\rightarrow 2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The lines falling in the visible region comprise Balmer series. Hence the third line would be $n_1=2, n_2=5$ i.e. $5 \\rightarrow 2$",
    "image": null
  },
